hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18933","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Mabad ibn Khalid, he said: I heard Harithah ibn Wahb, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Give charity, for soon a man will walk with his charity, and the one to whom it is offered will say: Had you brought it yesterday, I would have accepted it, but now I have no need of it, so he will find no one to accept it."
"18934","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Wahb al-Khuzai, he said: I prayed with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the Zuhr and Asr prayers at Mina, when the people were most numerous and most secure, two rakahs."
"18935","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mabad ibn Khalid, he said: I heard Harithah ibn Wahb al-Khuzai saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Shall I inform you of the people of Paradise: every weak one deemed weak, if he swears by Allah, He fulfills it for him. Shall I inform you of the people of Hell: every harsh, coarse, arrogant one."
"18936","Waki narrated to us, from Shubah, from Mabad ibn Khalid, he said: I heard Harithah ibn Wahb, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Give charity, for soon one of you will go out with his charity and find no one to accept it from him."
"18937","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mabad ibn Khalid, from Harithah ibn Wahb, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Shall I tell you of the people of Paradise: every weak one deemed weak, if he swears by Allah, He fulfills it for him. Shall I tell you of the people of Hell: every cruel, harsh, arrogant one."
"18938","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq narrating from Harithah ibn Wahb al-Khuzai, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led us in prayer, when we were most numerous and most secure, at Mina, two rakahs."
"18939","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mabad ibn Khalid, he said: I heard Harithah ibn Wahb al-Khuzai, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then he mentioned the hadith."
